{"text": "ra a UNITED STATES DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE\n: * | The Secretary of Commerce\nees | Washington, D.C, 20230\n\nMay 17, 2019\n\nThe Honorable Charles E. Schumer\nDemocratic Leader\nUnited States Senate\nWashington, DC 20510\n\nDear Mr. Leader:\n\nI am writing in response to your letter to the Bureau of Economic Analysis (BEA)\nregarding BEA\u2019s efforts to measure and publish information on the distributional measures of\nincome\n\nBEA\u2019s Office of the Chief Economist is leading research efforts to develop the means,\n\u2018methods, and processes necessary to publish regular measures of the distribution of personal\nincome. BEA anticipates publishing prototype measures within calendar year 2020, after which\nit will seek public comments on the proposed methodology. We believe this plan is consistent\nwith the language accompanying the Consolidated Appropriations Act of 2019.\n\nProducing regular and timely measures of the distribution of personal income presents\nsome challenges largely related to the coverage and timely availability of the source data ~ most\nnotably, the availability and access to timely tax data, As a result, BEA is exploring alternative\nmethods and data sources.\n\nRegarding new legislative authority and other resources to facilitate this work, we have\nno requests at this time. However, we do expect to have a much clearer idea of the full set of\nrequirements for this work after completing the development of prototype statistics and\nidentifying an approach for ongoing production of the distribution of personal income. We will\nshare our findings upon completion of this work.\n\nFinally, I would like to thank you for your words of commendation for the\nprofessionalism and expertise of BEA\u2019s staff. I fully concur with this sentiment.\n\nSincerely,\n\n(Joel Lew\n\nWilbur Ross",
